[h2][b]Save state[/b][/h2]

[b]No[/b] (removing the extension does not break saves).

[h2][b]Usage[/b][/h2]

Open the map, select a player-owned station, and click the [b]Production Overview[/b] tab in the info panel (left or right side).

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-StationProductionOverview/refs/heads/main/docs/images/production_overview_tab.png[/img]

[h2]Live vs Estimated mode[/h2]

The dropdown switches between [b]Current (live state)[/b] (actual running rates; Modules column shows [b]active/total[/b]) and [b]Estimated (all modules active)[/b] (every module running, with the workforce bonus of the workers present now).

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-StationProductionOverview/refs/heads/main/docs/images/production_calculation_type_dropdown.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-StationProductionOverview/refs/heads/main/docs/images/production_estimated.png[/img]

[h2]Ware groups[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]Products[/b]: produced here, not consumed on-site.
[*] [b]Intermediates[/b]: produced and consumed internally.
[*] [b]Resources[/b]: consumed as inputs, not produced on-site.
[/list]
Workforce-only consumer goods (food, medicine, etc.) also appear here unless produced on-site (from version 9.00.08).

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-StationProductionOverview/refs/heads/main/docs/images/workforce_resource_usage.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-StationProductionOverview/refs/heads/main/docs/images/workforce_resource_production.png[/img]

[h2]Planned module preview[/h2]

If the construction plan has unbuilt modules, a delta row per ware shows [b](+N)[/b] planned modules and their additional production/consumption.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-StationProductionOverview/refs/heads/main/docs/images/planned_modules.png[/img]

[h2]Empire balance[/h2]

Enable the [b]Show empire balance[/b] checkbox (single-station view only) to show an [i]All stations:[/i] sub-row per Product, Intermediate and Resource with empire-wide production, consumption, and a coloured balance (green = surplus, red = deficit). Resources without any production method (mined ores and gases, raw scrap) get no such row, since no station can produce them. Respects Live / Estimated mode.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-StationProductionOverview/refs/heads/main/docs/images/show_empire_balance.png[/img]

[h2]Storage[/h2]

Enable the [b]Show storage[/b] checkbox to add a [i]Stock:[/i] sub-row under each ware: the amount on the station, the storage allocated to it, and when it runs empty or full at the current balance, coloured red, yellow or green by the time left (limits set in the options). A [b]Storage[/b] group at the end lists each storage type with its fill level, the hourly volume produced and consumed, and its capacity. A storage type the station needs but does not have is shown in red, in the Storage group and under each ware that needs it.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-StationProductionOverview/refs/heads/main/docs/images/show_storage.png[/img]

[h2]Module states[/h2]

In Live mode a ware is highlighted when any of its modules is destroyed, damaged, hacked, paused, waiting for resources or waiting for storage; the counts per state appear as a sub-row or a tooltip.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-StationProductionOverview/refs/heads/main/docs/images/module_states.png[/img]

[h2]Extensions options[/h2]

[b]Options Menu > Extension options > Station Production Overview[/b]:
[list]
[*] [b]Data Refresh Interval[/b] (1-10, default 3): UI ticks to reuse cached data before recomputing. Lower = more responsive, higher = less CPU.
[*] [b]Sort by[/b]: wares by [b]Name[/b] or by [b]Balance (deficit first)[/b].
[*] [b]Red: empty or full within[/b] (1-24 hours, default 2) and [b]Yellow: empty or full within[/b] (default 6): a stock forecast below the red limit is shown in red, below the yellow limit in yellow, otherwise in green. The red limit cannot exceed the yellow one.
[*] [b]Show errors as sub-rows[/b]: if checked, the error states of modules are shown as sub-rows under each ware instead of tooltips on the ware name.
[*] [b]Ignore errors[/b]:
[list]
[*] [b]Modules without resources[/b]: if checked, this module state is ignored when identifying production issues,
[*] [b]Modules waiting for storage[/b]: if checked, this module state is ignored when identifying production issues,
[*] [b]Paused modules[/b]: if checked, modules you paused yourself are not shown as an issue.
[/list]
[*] [b]Synchronize with Production Stations Tab[/b]: if enabled, the data refresh interval and error handling settings are kept in sync between this mod and the [b]Production Stations Tab[/b] mod (if installed).
[*] [b]Debug Level[/b]: None, Debug or Trace; writes the mod's diagnostics to the game log.
[/list]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-StationProductionOverview/refs/heads/main/docs/images/options.png[/img]

[h2]Sector Production Overview[/h2]

Select a sector in the map to get the same [b]Production Overview[/b] tab listing all player-owned production stations in that sector. With more than one station, a [b]Sector total[/b] block first sums every ware over all of them.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-StationProductionOverview/refs/heads/main/docs/images/sector_production_overview_tab.png[/img]

